Relevant columns and potential usage for the question

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES  
  – "id": unique key of every historical node (needed to compare with current nodes)  
  – "username": mapper name we have to aggregate on  
  – "all_tags": VARIANT containing (key,value) pairs; we must locate amenity = ‘hospital’ / ‘clinic’ / ‘doctors’  
  – "latitude", "longitude": numeric strings that allow us to restrict the search to the bounding‑box  
  – "osm_timestamp": lets us see when the node existed (optional)  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES  
  – "id": current node id; used to detect that a historical node is missing today  
  – "all_tags": may still contain amenity tags (useful for spot checks)  
  – "latitude", "longitude": can help confirm the bbox  

Typical conditions that will be combined  
1. Bounding box  
   "latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921  
   "longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246  

2. Amenity tag (after flattening "all_tags")  
   tag.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'            AND  
   tag.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( 'hospital' , 'clinic' , 'doctors' )  

3. Missing from current data  
   hn."id" NOT IN ( SELECT pn."id" FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES pn )  

4. Aggregation  
   GROUP BY "username" ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC LIMIT 3  


Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries  
(each limited to 20 rows; adjust to taste)

```sql
--Description: 1) Quick look at raw historical nodes (first 20)
SELECT * 
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Peek at the structure of the VARIANT column “all_tags”
SELECT hn."id",
       hn."all_tags"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Flatten “all_tags” to see the internal (key,value) pairs
SELECT hn."id",
       tag.value:"key"   ::STRING AS "key",
       tag.value:"value" ::STRING AS "value"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) List distinct amenity values that appear in historical nodes (quick profiling)
SELECT DISTINCT tag.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_value"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
WHERE tag.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Fetch historical nodes in the specified rectangle (no tag filter yet)
SELECT hn."id",
       hn."username",
       hn."latitude",
       hn."longitude"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn
WHERE hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Historical nodes in bbox whose amenity is hospital / clinic / doctors
SELECT hn."id",
       hn."username",
       tag.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
WHERE tag.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND tag.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( 'hospital', 'clinic', 'doctors' )
  AND hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Verify which of those nodes are still present in current PLANET_NODES
SELECT hn."id" AS "hist_id",
       pn."id" AS "planet_id_match"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES  hn
LEFT JOIN GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES pn
       ON hn."id" = pn."id"
WHERE hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Bbox + amenity nodes that no longer exist in PLANET_NODES (id IS NULL)
SELECT hn."id",
       hn."username",
       tag.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn
LEFT JOIN GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES pn
       ON hn."id" = pn."id"
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
WHERE pn."id" IS NULL
  AND tag.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND tag.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( 'hospital', 'clinic', 'doctors' )
  AND hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Counts per username of the above disappearing amenity nodes
SELECT hn."username",
       COUNT(*) AS "disappeared_amenity_nodes"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn
LEFT JOIN GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES pn
       ON hn."id" = pn."id"
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
WHERE pn."id" IS NULL
  AND tag.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND tag.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( 'hospital', 'clinic', 'doctors' )
  AND hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
GROUP BY hn."username"
ORDER BY "disappeared_amenity_nodes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final result candidate – top three usernames with most vanished amenity nodes
SELECT hn."username",
       COUNT(*) AS "lost_nodes"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.HISTORY_NODES hn
LEFT JOIN GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES pn
       ON hn."id" = pn."id"
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => hn."all_tags") tag
WHERE pn."id" IS NULL
  AND tag.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
  AND tag.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ( 'hospital', 'clinic', 'doctors' )
  AND hn."latitude"  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND hn."longitude" BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
GROUP BY hn."username"
ORDER BY "lost_nodes" DESC
LIMIT 3;
```
